  "language": "en",
  "text": "out of 10 times the truth about perfectionism is that it's just procrastination in disguise. And the reason why I say 9 out of 10 times is because there is that small percentage of people who utilize perfectionism specifically in content as a high standard to work after, meaning that they're still moving and doing necessary steps to achieve that goal. But for the majority of the population utilize perfectionism as a form of creating the high standard, but they that into this obstacle that this false narrative that's created around it it's ultimately just procrastination.",
